<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Naseby</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1645</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-english-civil-war">First English Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Naseby was fought on 14 June 1645 in Northamptonshire between the main Royalist army of Charles I and Parliament's New Model Army under Sir Thomas Fairfax and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell">Oliver Cromwell</a>. The Parliamentarians destroyed the Royalist infantry and captured the king's baggage, including letters that damaged his cause. It was the decisive battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-english-civil-war">First English Civil War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-naseby.jpg" alt="Battle of Naseby" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Naseby,_hand-coloured_copper_engraving.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
